  ["The stateless ingestion API, because it can't run more than one instance behind a load balancer and therefore caps the platform's throughput entirely.",
   "Kafka consumer groups, which can never have more than one consumer each.",
   "The correlation-id middleware, which serializes all requests."],
  "Deep dive from the walkthrough: \"How do you scale this to 10x the partners?\"\n\nKafka scales horizontally by adding consumer instances per group, up to the partition count. The ingestion API scales behind a load balancer because it's stateless. The bottleneck to watch is the single Postgres instance backing the outbox: past a certain write volume, sharding or read replicas become a real conversation, worth naming even if you wouldn't build it on day one.\n\nRelated trade-offs to say out loud: at-least-once plus idempotent consumers over exactly-once; orchestration (Temporal) for the core pipeline but choreography for subscriber reactions, since one workflow controlling every downstream team would recreate the coupling the platform exists to remove.",
